    "result_text": "The test passes. The change is complete.\n\n## What I built\n\nA **home-screen dashboard** at `/dashboard` summarising all three entities, implemented full-stack and purely additively (all new files, nothing existing edited except adding one repository method):\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V7__invoice_status_index.sql`: an additive index on `invoice.status` supporting the outstanding-total aggregate.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST):\n- `rest/api/dashboard.GET.yml` + `DashboardGet.java` \u2014 a new `GET /api/dashboard` endpoint under `/api/` so it bypasses the SPA fallback.\n- `DashboardView.java` \u2014 the read-only aggregate DTO (`clientsCount`, `projectsCount`, `outstandingTotal`).\n- `InvoiceRepository.sumUnpaidAmount()` \u2014 a `COALESCE(SUM(...), 0)` query summing only `UNPAID` invoice amounts (the money still owed). Counts come from the injected `ClientRepository.count()` / `ProjectRepository.count()`.\n\n**Front-end** (all new files):\n- `routes/dashboard.tsx` \u2014 the page (route tree regenerates from it).\n- `features/dashboard/nav.slot.tsx` \u2014 its nav link (`data-testid=\"nav-dashboard\"`), filling the `app.nav` slot.\n- `features/dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` \u2014 reads `/api/dashboard` via `useQuery` under the `['dashboard']` key (server data never copied into state), rendering `dashboard-clients-count`, `dashboard-projects-count`, and `dashboard-outstanding-total` (formatted to 2 decimals, matching the invoice-amount convention).\n\nThe spec's fixture (2 clients, 2 projects, invoices 100 UNPAID + 50 PAID + 200 UNPAID) yields `2`, `2`, and `300.00` \u2014 all three assertions pass.",
